   "sec": 21.6,
   "heard": "The last job is the one people rush. The economy needs figures, not one line. Nearly half of Indians work in farming. Nearly half of that farming depends on rain. Kharif crops give almost half the year's grain. A good monsoon fills the reservoirs. And a weak one shows up in prices. This October, the Reserve Bank named the deficient monsoon as a pressure on food prices."
